		<item>
		<title>LEGOLAND New York Parking &#038; Food Guide</title>
		<link>https://www.toysnbricks.com/legoland-new-york-parking-food-guide/</link>
					<comments>https://www.toysnbricks.com/legoland-new-york-parking-food-guide/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Contributor Writer]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 01:28:08 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[General]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[LEGO & LEGOLAND News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[LEGOLAND Resources]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.toysnbricks.com/?p=113798</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="930" height="813" src="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York-Dining-Restaurant-Options-Food-Items-Snacks.jpg" class="attachment-post-thumbnail size-post-thumbnail wp-post-image" alt="LEGOLAND New York Dining &amp; Restaurant Options Food Items Snacks" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York-Dining-Restaurant-Options-Food-Items-Snacks.jpg 930w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York-Dining-Restaurant-Options-Food-Items-Snacks-300x262.jpg 300w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York-Dining-Restaurant-Options-Food-Items-Snacks-768x671.jpg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 930px) 100vw, 930px" /></p>
<p>The resort doesn’t allow home-cooked meals, so you’ll need to eat at one of the available food spots.</p>
<p>© Toys N Bricks: 2009-Present. <a href="https://www.toysnbricks.com/legoland-new-york-parking-food-guide/">LEGOLAND New York Parking &#038; Food Guide</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.toysnbricks.com"></a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter wp-image-106330 size-full" src="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/LEGOLAND-New-York-Front-Gate-Entrance-Main-Banner-Logo-3.jpg" alt="" width="1346" height="896" srcset="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/LEGOLAND-New-York-Front-Gate-Entrance-Main-Banner-Logo-3.jpg 1346w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/LEGOLAND-New-York-Front-Gate-Entrance-Main-Banner-Logo-3-300x200.jpg 300w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/LEGOLAND-New-York-Front-Gate-Entrance-Main-Banner-Logo-3-1024x682.jpg 1024w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/LEGOLAND-New-York-Front-Gate-Entrance-Main-Banner-Logo-3-768x511.jpg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1346px) 100vw, 1346px" /><br />
<span style="font-weight: 400;">The resort doesn’t allow home-cooked meals, so you’ll need to eat at one of the available food spots. This is one area most first-time visitors overlook when planning their trip. For that reason, I’ve put together this <a href="https://merlin.prf.hn/click/camref:1100l5xoXG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LEGOLAND New York</a> parking &amp; food guide to help you understand the food options available.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Like food, parking isn’t free. You’ll have to pay for it, but how you go about it is what differentiates you from most new resort-goers. And if you have a small RV, you can drive it to the park as well. For larger vehicles, you’ll have to find a parking spot outside the resort.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Note that parking isn’t restricted to the park alone. You can also park your vehicle at the hotel and, even better, receive complimentary parking. This guide will tell you everything you need to know about parking and food at <a href="https://merlin.prf.hn/click/camref:1100l5xoXG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LEGOLAND New York</a></span>.</p>
<p><em>Shown below is the Captain&#8217;s Grill Menu at <span style="font-weight: 400;"><a href="https://merlin.prf.hn/click/camref:1100l5xoXG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LEGOLAND New York</a></span> Brickbeard&#8217;s Food Market.</em></p>
