<h2><span style="font-weight: 400;">The LEGOLAND New York Parking Guide</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">I recommend you book your parking online, as that approach offers the most ease. You might not get discount deals like tickets, if that’s what you are thinking. But that gives you one less thing to worry about when you arrive at the resort.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">As mentioned earlier, you can park at the resort or at the hotel. The parking options to consider are:</span></p>
<h3><span style="font-weight: 400;">Pre-paid LEGOLAND Parking</span></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">There are ways to pre-pay for parking at the resort, and they are:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Via online purchases</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">At the Park Admissions Ticket Window</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">At the Guest Experience Center just inside the park entrance</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Whichever approach you use, you’ll get a one-day parking pass. Once you receive it, you can park your vehicle and scan your pass at the resort’s Exit Toll.</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Buy Tickets &amp; Book LEGOLAND Hotel Stays at the Official LEGOLAND Site: </strong><a href="https://merlin.prf.hn/click/camref:1100l5xoXG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LEGOLAND New York</a></li>
</ul>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-full wp-image-113834 aligncenter" src="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York-Driving-School-Ride-Attraction-Banner-Logo.jpg" alt="" width="916" height="366" srcset="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York-Driving-School-Ride-Attraction-Banner-Logo.jpg 916w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York-Driving-School-Ride-Attraction-Banner-Logo-300x120.jpg 300w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York-Driving-School-Ride-Attraction-Banner-Logo-768x307.jpg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 916px) 100vw, 916px" /></p>
<h3><span style="font-weight: 400;">Preferred Parking</span></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">If you want a more VIP-like treatment, preferred parking is your best bet. With this option, you can reserve a dedicated parking space on the day of your visit. What I love even more is that preferred parking spaces are the closest to the park’s entrance, giving you easy access in and out.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Like the pre-paid parking option, you will have to scan your ticket at the exit toll when you leave. There are a few other things to consider, which are:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">The spaces for preferred parking are limited, even more limited than standard parking</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;"><span style="font-weight: 400;"><a href="https://merlin.prf.hn/click/camref:1100l5xoXG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LEGOLAND New York</a> offers preferred parking on a first-come, first-served basis</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">You can only book your preferred parking ticket online</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Note also that your vehicle must fit in the standard car parking space for this ticket to be valid.</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Buy Tickets &amp; Book LEGOLAND Hotel Stays at the Official LEGOLAND Site: </strong><a href="https://merlin.prf.hn/click/camref:1100l5xoXG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LEGOLAND New York</a></li>
</ul>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-full wp-image-113833 aligncenter" src="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-Driving-School-Ride-Attraction-Feature.webp" alt="" width="500" height="500" srcset="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-Driving-School-Ride-Attraction-Feature.webp 500w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-Driving-School-Ride-Attraction-Feature-300x300.webp 300w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-Driving-School-Ride-Attraction-Feature-150x150.webp 150w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /></p>
<h3><span style="font-weight: 400;">Pay As You Leave</span></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">I recommend purchasing your tickets online, but it isn’t a must. You can still drive down to the resort, have a splendid time with your family, and pay for parking on your way out. It’s an option you can consider if you don’t want to go through the hassle of purchasing your tickets online.</span></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400;">Guide For Passholders</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">As a passholder, you will receive free general parking any time you visit the resort, but you have to be at the preferred or premium level. You can also get up to a 50% discount on parking. Note that discounted parking is available online, and you may have to pre-purchase the ticket.</span></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Buy Tickets &amp; Book LEGOLAND Hotel Stays at the Official LEGOLAND Site: </strong><a href="https://merlin.prf.hn/click/camref:1100l5xoXG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LEGOLAND New York</a></li>
</ul>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-full wp-image-113835 aligncenter" src="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York-Annual-Passer-Banner-Logo.webp" alt="" width="840" height="560" srcset="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York-Annual-Passer-Banner-Logo.webp 840w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York-Annual-Passer-Banner-Logo-300x200.webp 300w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York-Annual-Passer-Banner-Logo-768x512.webp 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 840px) 100vw, 840px" /></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400;">Electric Vehicle Parking</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">This <a href="https://merlin.prf.hn/click/camref:1100l5xoXG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LEGOLAND New York</a> parking &amp; food guide will be incomplete if I don’t speak on electric vehicles. The impressive thing is that the park not only accommodates electric vehicles. It has also included 2 charging stations in Lot B. If you park at the hotel, you’ll find 4 charging stations, with considerations for disabled spots.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Speaking of considerations, you have to be considerate of other guests when using the charging stations. For that reason, the resort has the following:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">You can’t charge for more than 2 hours</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Overnight charging is unavailable</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">The parking spaces there are for charging only (once you are done, you are expected to move your vehicle)</span></li>
</ul>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-full wp-image-113733 aligncenter" src="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York.webp" alt="" width="800" height="800" srcset="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York.webp 800w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York-300x300.webp 300w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York-150x150.webp 150w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York-768x768.webp 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px" /></p>
<h2><span style="font-weight: 400;">Dining and Restaurants at LEGOLAND New York</span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Like its sister locations, <a href="https://merlin.prf.hn/click/camref:1100l5xoXG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LEGOLAND New York</a> has spots for quick bites and full meals. Two things I got from the resorts are speed and convenience. You can grab quick bites as you move from one ride to another. Even better, the dining options are family-friendly.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">As of this writing, I’ve counted a dozen dining spots at the resort and more at the hotel. I wouldn’t go searching for full meals at the resort. The menu is mostly snacks, with a few offering light meals.</span></p>
<h3><span style="font-weight: 400;">Quick Snack Spots at the Resort</span></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">In no particular order, a few spots you can consider on your visit are:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;"><b>Ben’s Soft Pretzel’s:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> You’ll find this spot at Bricktopia in the theme park. It is the go-to option if you want fresh, soft, delicious, and hand-made pretzels. Even better, you can get them in different flavors.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;"><b>Food Carts:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> This option is perfect if you are waiting for a ride. The food carts contain snacks, treats, and drinks, and you’ll find them in several locations. These include Pirates Parlor, What’s Poppin’, Jester’ Fair, and City Scoops.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;"><b>Granny’s Apple Fries:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> If you’ve been in <a href="https://merlin.prf.hn/click/camref:1100l5xoXM" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LEGOLAND Florida</a> </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">(check out <a href="https://www.toysnbricks.com/legoland-florida-ultimate-guide-2027-update/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">our ultimate 2027 guide</a>)</span><span style="font-weight: 400;">, you will know that Granny’s Apple Fries is one of the OGs when it comes to dining options in the resort. It’s where you can expect the crisp, seasonal, New York apples dusted in sugar and cinnamon. You also have the vanilla cream dipping sauce to go with it.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;"><b>Wizard’s Frozen Wonders:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> This spot is where you satisfy your sweet tooth. It is one of the foremost spots for ice cream.</span></li>
<li><strong>Buy Tickets &amp; Book LEGOLAND Hotel Stays at the Official LEGOLAND Site: </strong><a href="https://merlin.prf.hn/click/camref:1100l5xoXG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LEGOLAND New York</a></li>
</ul>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-full wp-image-113832 aligncenter" src="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York-Dining-Restaurant-Options-Food-Items-Snacks.jpg" alt="" width="930" height="813" srcset="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York-Dining-Restaurant-Options-Food-Items-Snacks.jpg 930w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York-Dining-Restaurant-Options-Food-Items-Snacks-300x262.jpg 300w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/LEGOLAND-New-York-Dining-Restaurant-Options-Food-Items-Snacks-768x671.jpg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 930px) 100vw, 930px" /></p>
<h3><span style="font-weight: 400;">Theme Park Restaurants to Check Out</span></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">For casual dining, you can consider the following spots:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;"><b>Brickolini’s Pizza and Pasta:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> For freshly made pasta, salad, and pizza, this spot is my go-to option. It is one of the most visited food spots in the resort, and for good reason.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;"><b>Smokey’s Brick-B-Que:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> If you want that American-style barbecue, you have to check out this spot. Even better, the spot offers limited-time deals, and the deals are available while supplies last.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;"><b>Royal Feast: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Hand-pressed burgers, cheeseburger meals, and kids’ chicken tenders are the hallmark of this food spot.</span></li>
<li><strong>Buy Tickets &amp; Book LEGOLAND Hotel Stays at the Official LEGOLAND Site: </strong><a href="https://merlin.prf.hn/click/camref:1100l5xoXG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LEGOLAND New York</a></li>
</ul>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-full wp-image-112695 aligncenter" src="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/LEGOLAND-New-York-Restaurant-Dining-Options.jpg" alt="" width="922" height="616" srcset="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/LEGOLAND-New-York-Restaurant-Dining-Options.jpg 922w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/LEGOLAND-New-York-Restaurant-Dining-Options-300x200.jpg 300w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/LEGOLAND-New-York-Restaurant-Dining-Options-768x513.jpg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 922px) 100vw, 922px" /></p>
<h3><span style="font-weight: 400;">More Dining Options At the Hotel</span></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">For me, the hotel is the only place you can get proper family-friendly full meals. They are the main sit-down options where you relax and dine without the bustle of jumping from one ride to another.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The 3 dining options available are:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;"><b>Bricks Family Restaurant:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> This spot offers buffet-style dining with a rotating themed menu each night. Even better, the kids can enjoy new LEGO adventures every evening. As for the cost, you can expect to spend at least $9.99 for kids’ meals.</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Skyline Bar</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Skyline Cantina</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">If you are at the poolside, you can grab refreshing drinks and snacks at the Sandbar. The hotel also has pizza room service that delivers pizza directly to your room</span><span style="font-weight: 400;">.</span></p>
